 # Online Appointment and Scheduling System
 
-Book appointments without double-booking. Work in progress.
+Book appointments without double-booking. Every person registers, logs in, and sees only **their own** schedule.
+
+![Dashboard](docs/dashboard.png)
+
+- **Frontend:** React + Vite (`client/`)
+- **Backend:** Node.js REST API (`server/`), built-in `http` and `node:sqlite`, no npm packages needed
+- **Database:** SQLite file created automatically at `server/data.db`
+
+## Requirements
+Node.js **22.13 or newer** (`node -v` to check). Node 22 prints an "experimental" warning for SQLite. That is normal.
+
+## Run it (two terminals)
+
+    # terminal 1: API on http://localhost:3001
+    cd server
+    npm start
+
+    # terminal 2: React app on http://localhost:5173
+    cd client
+    npm install
+    npm run dev
+
+Open http://localhost:5173, choose **Create an account**, then book your first appointment.
+
+## Run the tests
+
+    cd server
+    npm test
+
+## Features
+- **Register, log in, log out.** Each account has its own private appointments. Sessions last 7 days.
+- **Double-booking protection.** Booking over an existing appointment is refused, and the app suggests the next free start time. Back-to-back appointments are allowed.
+- **Day timeline.** See the day from 8 AM to 6 PM. Click any free slot to book it, or click an appointment to edit it. Use the arrows or the date picker to change day.
+- **Summary cards.** Appointments today (with a "how full is the day" bar), upcoming count, your next appointment, and the next free slot today.
+- **Appointment list.** Search (press **/**), filter by status, sort any column, export to CSV, and mark appointments completed, cancelled or reopened.
+- **Dark mode**, remembered between visits, and a **mobile layout** where the table becomes cards.
+
+| Overlap warning | Dark mode | Mobile |
+|---|---|---|
+| ![Overlap](docs/overlap-warning.png) | ![Dark](docs/dark-mode.png) | ![Mobile](docs/mobile.png) |
+
+## Booking rules
+- Working hours are 08:00 to 18:00. An appointment must finish by 18:00.
+- Start times are in 15 minute steps. Lengths are 15, 30, 45, 60, 90 or 120 minutes.
+- Cancelled appointments free up their time. Reopening one is refused if the time is taken again.
+
+## API
+| Method | Path | What it does |
+|---|---|---|
+| POST | /api/register | Create an account and log in |
+| POST | /api/login | Log in (sets a cookie) |
+| POST | /api/logout | Log out (clears the cookie) |
+| GET | /api/me | Who is logged in (401 if nobody) |
+| GET | /api/config | Types, statuses, durations and working hours |
+| GET | /api/appointments | List **your** appointments, sorted by date and time |
+| POST | /api/appointments | Book one (409 on overlap, with a suggested start time) |
+| PUT | /api/appointments/:id | Edit one |
+| PATCH | /api/appointments/:id | Change only the status |
+| DELETE | /api/appointments/:id | Delete one |
+| GET | /api/day?date=2026-11-10 | One day: appointments, how full it is, next free slot (`&after=HH:MM&duration=30`) |
+
+## How it works
+1. The form sends JSON to the API. `validate.js` checks every field and the working hours.
+2. Times are stored as minutes since midnight, so an overlap is a simple comparison (`time.js`).
+3. Before saving, the server looks for a live appointment that overlaps (`findConflict` in `db.js`). If one exists it answers 409 and suggests the next free start.
+4. Every query filters by the logged-in user, so nobody can read, edit or delete another person's appointments.
+
+## Security notes
+- Passwords are hashed with scrypt and a random salt. The plain password is never stored.
+- The login cookie is `HttpOnly` and `SameSite=Lax`. The database keeps only a hash of the session token.
+- After 10 wrong passwords for one username, login is blocked for 15 minutes.
+- For a real deployment, serve over HTTPS and add the `Secure` flag to the cookie.
+
+## Ideas to extend
+Admin role who can see every schedule, email or SMS reminders, recurring appointments, a public booking page for clients, change password.
